From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:25:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 37/54] Make OTLP exports wait for the application network
 policy

The periodic metrics reader starts exporting before the configuration owner has
published the application network policy. PolicyExporter::export failed at once with
"application network policy is unavailable", and because the metrics use delta
temporality the counts in that export were lost. A test that waited for those counts
then failed after its 60 second deadline.

An export now waits, for at most 10 seconds, for the policy to be published. It
subscribes to policy changes before it checks, so a publication in between is not
missed. Any other denial, such as a restricting policy, still fails at once. SDK
worker threads drive export futures outside a Tokio runtime, so a timer thread bounds
the wait instead of a Tokio timer.

The unit tests start an export before the policy exists and publish while it waits:
an unrestricted policy lets the export through and a restricting one denies it
without exporting. A third test checks that the wait ends when no policy arrives.
